fseek ( fp, -recsize, SEEK_CUR ) ;

Here, -recsize moves the pointer back by recsize bytes from the current position. SEEK_CUR is a macro defined in “stdio.h”. Similarly, the following fseek( ) would place the pointer beyond the last record in the file.

